{
  "name": "neverball",
  "title": "NEVERBALL (Robert Kooima and the Neverball team; 1.6.0, 2014: C on SDL 2, OpenGL, SDL2_ttf over FreeType, libvorbisfile, libpng, libjpeg)",
  "dir": "corpus/neverball-1.6.0",
  "fetch": "curl -sL https://neverball.org/neverball-1.6.0.tar.gz | tar -xz -C corpus (sha256 73fe63cc...a88fa0; SHA-512 and size as NetBSD pkgsrc's games/neverball/distinfo); libpng 1.6.16 (https://download.sourceforge.net/libpng/libpng-1.6.16.tar.gz, sha256 02f96b6b...2073ad); libjpeg 6b and zlib 1.1.3 as for chromium-bsu; SDL2_ttf 2.0.12 (https://www.libsdl.org/projects/SDL_ttf/release/SDL2_ttf-2.0.12.tar.gz, sha256 87286054...356f6e), libogg 1.3.2 and libvorbis 1.3.4 (downloads.xiph.org/releases/, sha256 e19ee347...a654692 and eee09a0a...a1ecb, as Xiph's SHA256SUMS list them), FreeType 2.3.11 as for chromium-bsu",
  "_build": "The Makefile's BALL_OBJS with its defaults (ENABLE_FS=stdio as for mapc, tilt_null, hmd_null, ENABLE_NLS=0), its -std=c99 and release flags. Libraries as their own builds list them: SDL2_ttf's SDL_ttf.c; libvorbis's libvorbis_la_SOURCES and libvorbisfile_la_SOURCES (lib/Makefile.am); libogg's src/ (its configure's ogg/config_types.h, run in the oracle, in corpus/libogg-1.3.2-generated); FreeType with chromium-bsu's configuration (its generated ftconfig.h/ftmodule.h and per-unit defines); libpng, libjpeg and zlib as for mapc. GL extensions asked of gl.js: the three glext_init asserts (ARB_multitexture, ARB_vertex_buffer_object, ARB_point_parameters) and ARB_point_sprite, which part.c uses. libvorbis is compiled without __i386__ (its units only): os.h then takes its C rounding for vorbis_ftoi instead of x87's fistl, as an x86-64 build does -- the choice mapc's levels were held to. SDL_ttf.c without the i386 macro too, as FreeType's own units: ftconfig.h's FT_MulFix inline is then FreeType's C rather than its x87 assembly (FT_MulFix_i386), with the same rounding.",
